{"availability":"available","full":"kubebao/openbao-operator","name":"openbao-operator","description":"The OpenBao Operator manages the lifecycle of OpenBao clusters on Kubernetes. It handles the orchestration complexity, PKI, backups, upgrades, and secure multi-tenancy, so you can focus on consuming secrets.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Go","stars":30,"forks":5,"created":"2026-01-03T19:19:17Z","updated":"2026-10-12T03:03:51Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://docs.kubebao.org/","topics":["kubernetes","kubernetes-operator","openbao","secret-management"],"demo":"https://dc-tec.github.io/openbao-operator/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T06:28:03.136Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T06:28:03.136Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T06:28:03.136Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T03:37:49.384Z","stars":29,"forks":3},{"at":"2026-10-12T06:28:03.136Z","stars":30,"forks":5}],"technologies":["Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Secure lifecycle management for OpenBao on Kubernetes.","Pre-GA Release: OpenBao Operator is intended for real deployments, but the CRD API remains v1alpha1, minor releases may introduce breaking changes, and support is best-effort for the latest stable line only. For production, use the Hardened profile, keep admission enforcement enabled, pin explicit versions, and validate upgrades in staging.","OpenBao Operator is a Kubernetes operator for OpenBao that automates lifecycle management: provisioning, TLS, backups/restores, upgrades, horizontal read scaling, and multi-tenancy controls."],"features":["Two-Controller Architecture: Separate controller and provisioner components with least-privilege RBAC boundaries.","Security Profiles with Guardrails: Development vs Hardened, enforced by admission policies to prevent insecure combinations.","Self-Init + OIDC Bootstrap: OpenBao self-initialization, with optional JWT/OIDC bootstrap via spec.selfInit.oidc.enabled.","TLS, Your Way: Operator-managed TLS with rotation, external TLS, and ACME mode where OpenBao owns certificates (with ACME challenge Service support).","Streaming Raft Backups: Snapshot streaming to S3/GCS/Azure with retention controls (no local staging)."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dc-tec/openbao-operator/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"aa380c21fab25f91ae40df961311de15b66f17200a21604a445efdf1f41e70a4","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:49.556Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:49.556Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Secure lifecycle management for OpenBao on Kubernetes.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dc-tec/openbao-operator/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[{"text":"Pre-GA Release: OpenBao Operator is intended for real deployments, but the CRD API remains v1alpha1, minor releases may introduce breaking changes, and support is best-effort for the latest stable line only. For production, use the Hardened profile, keep admission enforcement enabled, pin explicit versions, and validate upgrades in staging.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dc-tec/openbao-operator/blob/main/README.md"}],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"aa380c21fab25f91ae40df961311de15b66f17200a21604a445efdf1f41e70a4","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dc-tec/openbao-operator/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:49.557Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-08T22:46:57Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dc-tec/openbao-operator/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:49.557Z","hash":"aa380c21fab25f91ae40df961311de15b66f17200a21604a445efdf1f41e70a4","originalBytes":7268,"storedBytes":7268,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["openbao","operator","documentation","model","compatibility","contributing","guide","read","tls","upgrades","admission","boundaries","production","release","security","see","support","backups","bootstrap","cluster","controller","license","mode","multi-tenancy","multi-tenant","namespace","policies","rbac"